* LM386N audio amplifier: +6 V supply, gain 20, 8-ohm speaker
* Application topology based on TI LM386 datasheet, section 9.2.1.
* https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/lm386.pdf
* Includes an APPROXIMATE educational behavioral model, NOT a TI model.
* Gain pins 1 and 8 must remain open with this fixed-gain model.

.PARAM V_SUPPLY=6
.PARAM R_LOAD=8
.PARAM V_INPUT=50m

* Single positive supply: pin 6 = +6 V, pin 4 = ground.
V_SUPPLY VCC 0 DC {V_SUPPLY}
C_DECOUPLE VCC 0 100n
C_BULK VCC 0 100u

* 1 kHz test tone; 10k volume pot at its midpoint (50% voltage).
* V_INPUT is peak amplitude, not peak-to-peak.
V_AUDIO Audio_In 0 DC 0 AC 1 SIN(0 {V_INPUT} 1k)
C_INPUT Audio_In Pot_Top 1u
R_VOL_TOP Pot_Top Input_Plus 5k
R_VOL_BOTTOM Input_Plus 0 5k

* Physical DIP pin order: 1 gain, 2 in-, 3 in+, 4 GND,
* 5 output, 6 supply, 7 bypass, 8 gain.
X_AMP Gain_1 0 Input_Plus 0 IC_Out VCC Bypass Gain_8 LM386_GAIN20_APPROX
C_BYPASS Bypass 0 10u

* Output rests near half the supply; coupling cap blocks speaker DC.
* Electrolytic positive lead faces pin 5 (IC_Out).
C_OUTPUT IC_Out Speaker 250u
R_SPEAKER Speaker 0 {R_LOAD}

* Output stabilization network, mounted close to pin 5 and ground.
R_ZOBEL IC_Out Zobel 10
C_ZOBEL Zobel 0 50n

* Fixed-gain approximation: 20 V/V, 300 kHz small-signal pole,
* half-supply output bias, assumed 1.2 V rail headroom and 0.2-ohm Rout.
* These are illustrative assumptions, not a model of a particular suffix.
* Does NOT predict THD, current limiting, thermal behavior, supply current,
* slew limiting, PSRR, oscillation, or gain-pin/bypass-cap behavior.
.SUBCKT LM386_GAIN20_APPROX G1 INM INP GND OUT VS BYP G8
R_INP INP GND 50k
R_INM INM GND 50k
E_GAIN Gain_Node GND INP INM 20
R_POLE Gain_Node Filtered 1k
C_POLE Filtered GND 530.5p
B_OUTPUT Internal GND V=min(max(V(VS,GND)/2+V(Filtered,GND),1.2),V(VS,GND)-1.2)
R_OUTPUT Internal OUT 0.2
* Bypass bias provided only to give the external capacitor a DC operating point.
E_BYP Bypass_Ideal GND VS GND 0.5
R_BYP Bypass_Ideal BYP 15k
.ENDS LM386_GAIN20_APPROX

* Start transient after DC operating point; observe the final few cycles.
.TRAN 2u 30m 0 2u
.AC DEC 50 10 1Meg
.PRINT TRAN V(Audio_In) V(Input_Plus) V(IC_Out) V(Speaker)
.PRINT AC VM(Speaker)
.END
